## Chrome session setup

This project drives an already-running, already-logged-in Chrome instance over CDP rather than
launching its own — attach, never launch, so the login session is a human's, not a throwaway one:

1. Start Chrome with remote debugging enabled and a dedicated profile, e.g.
   `google-chrome --remote-debugging-port=9333 --user-data-dir=~/.cache/{{ package_name }}-chrome`.
2. Log in manually, once, in that Chrome window.
3. Leave it running — `{{ package_name }}` connects to it via `connect_over_cdp`, never `.launch()`.
